# Enforce ESLint and Modern JS Practices

description: |
  All JavaScript (*.js) and TypeScript (*.ts) files must comply with the project's ESLint configuration and use ES6+ features.

file_matcher: ["**/*.js", "**/*.ts"]

instructions: |
  - Follow the ESLint rules as configured in the project's .eslintrc file.
  - Use ES6+ syntax (e.g., arrow functions, const/let instead of var, template literals).
  - Prefer named exports over default exports unless specified.
  - Write all code comments in English.
  - Avoid using deprecated or experimental browser APIs.
